' ============================================================================
'  chamber-the-crypt.cut -- entering a named hall.
'
'  One file per chamber, named `chamber-<slug>.cut`, so the eventual
'  board-position trigger is a lookup and not a special case. This is also the
'  shape a future per-cell trigger table would fire.
' ============================================================================

scene chamber-the-crypt
stage 2112x1632

show bg "bg/cut-hall.png" scale 8 at 0.5,0.5
cam 0.30,0.5 zoom 2.0

' A long lateral pan across the hall, so the room reads as WIDE. This is the
' one thing a still image cannot do on its own.
async pan to 0.72,0.5 over 9.0 ease inout

sfx "chamber-enter"
narrate "chamber.the-crypt"
caption "THE CRYPT" at 66,3 anchor c color gold fade 1.0

say "Three doors, and the one you came through has already closed."
say "Something in here counts to three."

' First visit only. The flag is persistent, so the second visit is quieter --
' which is the point of persistent flags in a roguelike.
if not flag.seen_crypt
    set seen_crypt = 1
    say "You have not been here before. It has been here the whole time."
end

waitall
scatter over 1.0
